Fixed bitcoind wallet setup for Bitcoin Core >= 31 (unnamed wallets removed): with an empty `wallet_name`, the miner now resolves a wallet at startup (the single loaded one, or one named "default"), routes wallet RPCs explicitly to it, keeps it loaded across bitcoind restarts, and fails fast when multiple wallets are loaded and no `wallet_name` is configured.
After migrating a miner wallet to Bitcoin Core >= 31, set `burnchain.wallet_name` to the wallet holding the miner's addresses (`migratewallet` can split it in two).
